COPY [v1:]name v2[:newname]
COPY [v1:]pattern v2
COPY [v1:]name|pattern [v2:]folder[/]
  Copies a file to drive v2 (B or B:), as newname or the same name; a
  pattern (*.CYB, T*, ????.COM, *.*) copies each file that fits.
  A folder there (UniDOS) as the target: the files go into it, same
  names - a folder is never written over.
  Any file the drive has (UniDOS's folder, a RAM disc's directory).
